WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.020
Did you spot all of these moments in the new
trailer for "Across the Spider-Verse?"

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.140
We're not horsing around here.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.510
Let us point to some of the small details
you might have missed.

00:00:10.973 --> 00:00:16.290
He might be on the road to a trip across dimensions,
but before he can start on that journey, Miles

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.320
still has some local small-time crooks to
deal with.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.680
But in classic Spider-Man fashion, these happen
to be villains with exceptionally wild powers.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.820
The walking, talking bread dispenser found
stealing from a convenience store is Johnathon

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.630
Ohnn, also known as the Spot.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:36.690
This is a bad guy covered in inter-dimensional
portals that make him a nightmare for any hero.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:42.130
In "Peter Parker, the Spectacular Spider-Man"
#98, Dr. Jonathon Ohnn is sucked into a strange

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:46.200
black portal and becomes a super-powered being
called The Spot.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.680
That comic marked the beginning of his career
as part of Peter Parker's rogues' gallery.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.050
He wasn't originally an enemy of Miles Morales,
but it's nothing new for the "Spider-Verse"

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.380
series to play fast and loose with its heroes
and villains.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.809
In a sequel that's already going to send Miles
slipping in and out of portals, seeing him

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:07.930
tackle someone who can create them at will
is guaranteed to spark some fantastic sequences.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.250
We can't wait to see them.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.010
In the first movie in the "Spider-Verse" series,
one thing was made abundantly clear:

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.196
"Anyone can wear the mask.

00:01:18.196 --> 00:01:20.540
You could wear the mask!"

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.630
Well, there's a whole bunch of new masks to
spot in the sequel's second trailer.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.990
While there are plenty of returning favorites
here to catch your eye, as well as some oddballs

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:34.160
like Spider-Horse, the trailer also gives
us our first good look at some of Miles' new allies.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:39.257
There's Jessica Drew, also known as Spider-Woman,
riding in on her bike while bearing a baby bump.

00:01:39.257 --> 00:01:44.439
There's also Hobart "Hobie" Brown, the Spider-Punk,
along with Pravitr Prabhakar, otherwise known

00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:46.409
as Spider-Man India.

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:51.240
Jessica Drew is a storied character from Marvel
Comics, but Spider-Punk and Spider-Man India

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.280
might be a little more obscure.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.750
The guitar-rocking hero Spider-Punk debuted
in 2014, and this version sounds like a Londoner,

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.800
unlike the New York-based rebel from the comics.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.810
Spider-Man India is based on a four-issue
run of comics that retells Spidey's story

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.440
in an Indian setting.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.379
Beyond them, one of the real winning shots
of the trailer involves the appearance of

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:14.349
Ben Reilly, the infamous Scarlet Spider.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:16.650
Two things set Ben apart from his contemporaries.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.430
First, he looks cool, sporting a stylish blue
hooded vest.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.019
Second, in the comics, he is actually a clone
of Peter Parker created by villain Miles Warren,

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:27.260
the Jackal.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.530
This means that there is a chance that this
Scarlet Spider is actually one of two Spider-Men

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.120
from the same dimension.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.459
Although Ben was created to be a villain and
replace Peter Parker, in the comics, he finds

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:40.420
himself compelled to fight for the forces
of good.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.130
Before long he becomes one of Peter's allies.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:49.196
Popping up in his first comic in 1975, the
Scarlet Spider became a huge part of Spider-Man lore.

00:02:49.196 --> 00:02:52.127
For a time, he was even considered the main
comic Spider-Man.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.709
This occurred when Norman Osborn convinced
the two web crawlers that Peter Parker was

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.040
in fact the actual clone.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:04.720
The two then switched places, and Ben took
over the mantle thinking he was the original superhero.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.950
It will be interesting to see how the filmmakers
adapt such a complicated and major part of

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.500
Spider-Man continuity for the world of "Spider-Verse"
– or if they go there at all.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.120
Facing issues like bad guys and bad grades,
it's understandable why Miles would take the

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.660
first chance he gets to get away from his
world and into another ... or ten.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.799
As revealed by Gwen, the Lobby is a creation
of Miguel O'Hara, a hero from a futuristic

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:32.769
world who has teamed up with the best bunch
of web-slingers he can find.

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:37.140
Unfortunately, it seems that Miles hasn't
made the list, for some reason or another.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.030
"You can never be part of this.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:44.220
And don't even get me started on Doctor Strange
and the little nerd back on Earth-199999."

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:48.780
Now, while this will no doubt get lovers of
the live-action MCU excited about the streams

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.769
crossing, it's worth noting that the numbers
don't quite add up in regard to the Earth

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:53.820
mentioned here.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:04:00.000
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
pegs the MCU we know as Earth-616.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.120
However, many more comics-focused fans see
the MCU as being set more accurately in Earth-199999.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:12.479
Could this be the first step in getting an
animated Tom Holland swinging alongside Miles Morales?

00:04:12.479 --> 00:04:14.529
In the spider-verse, anything is possible.

00:04:15.196 --> 00:04:15.900
"Peter!"

00:04:15.937 --> 00:04:16.937
"Yeah?

00:04:16.937 --> 00:04:18.829
Oh, sorry, did you mean me?"

00:04:19.163 --> 00:04:24.854
Speaking of Peter, the trailer sees Peter
B. Parker from the first movie making a welcome re-appearance.

00:04:24.854 --> 00:04:29.479
As expected, he is now a proud father to a
baby girl named May.

00:04:29.479 --> 00:04:33.160
Swinging through the air without a care in
the world, May "Mayday" Parker is based on

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.415
Spider-Girl, who debuted in 1997 as part of
a "What If?" story.

00:04:37.415 --> 00:04:42.669
A member of the MC2 universe, an alternative
future timeline, she is the super-powered

00:04:42.669 --> 00:04:44.759
daughter of Peter Parker.

00:04:44.759 --> 00:04:48.440
Given her age and Peter's brief appearance
in the trailer, we wonder if Peter will be

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.979
taking a back seat this time around, with
an even greater focus on Miles.

00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:56.949
Even though Peter has seemingly been accepted
into O'Hara's team of web slingers, it doesn't

00:04:56.949 --> 00:04:59.759
mean he'll be the most active member of the
team.

00:04:59.759 --> 00:05:04.130
He is a father now, after all, and there's
a high chance that he'll only appear alongside

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.917
his former protégé in a mentor capacity.

00:05:07.519 --> 00:05:11.889
As much as Miles appears to want to join the
new Spider-Club, it seems that there's a toll

00:05:11.889 --> 00:05:14.690
for entry that he might not be willing to
pay.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:21.266
As explained by Miguel O'Hara, also known
as Spider-Man 2099, being Spider-Man is a sacrifice.

00:05:21.266 --> 00:05:29.270
"You have a choice between saving one person
and saving every world."

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.120
Is the seeming threat to Miles' dad a double
bluff?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.949
It could be - but as any fan of Spider-Man
knows, losing a family member is inevitable

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:38.000
with this job.

00:05:39.086 --> 00:05:43.810
Closing off this eye-watering preview, there's
a chunkier dose of spider versus spider as

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:48.410
Miles and Miguel battle on what looks like
a futuristic bullet train with other Spider-Folk,

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.610
including Peter and Gwen, trailing closely
behind.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:55.630
Peter tells Miguel that this isn't what the
futuristic crime fighter promised, suggesting

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.290
that this fresh dose of power might've gone
to O'Hara's head.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.250
Whatever it is he has planned, though, Miles
isn't signing up for it.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.630
In what feels like a final battle moment that
you'd expect would be tucked away until the

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:11.009
film's release, Miles looks to be charging
up against Miguel and saying he's "going to

00:06:11.009 --> 00:06:12.069
do his own thing."

00:06:12.069 --> 00:06:17.060
The question is, what kind of ramifications
could that have on all the universes?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.610
If the MCU and "Into the Spider-Verse" have
taught us anything, it's that throwing things

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.130
out of interdimensional whack causes serious
problems.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:29.729
With that in mind, could the film end with
Miles' actions having a negative impact and

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:32.130
Miguel being in the right after all?

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:36.099
Given that this is the second part of a planned
trilogy, who can say?

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:39.840
Either way, our Spidey-Senses are well and
truly tingling.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.090
If we were to go over all the Spider-Man suits
we spotted in this trailer, it would take

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.090
all day.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.350
Nonetheless, it's worth mentioning that one
decidedly more equine version of the character

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.690
makes a blink-and-you-miss-it appearance just
before the preview ends.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:58.660
Right as the amusing Spidey-to-Spidey therapy
session gets interrupted by Miles and a giant

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:02.759
mass of Spider-People crashing through the
wall, viewers can see that one of them is

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:05.879
actually a horse wearing a Spider-Man mask.

00:07:05.879 --> 00:07:09.949
Because this is a comic book movie we're talking
about, this bizarre Spider-Horse actually

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:12.900
has canonical precedent in the source material.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.560
His name is Widow, and he gains his superpowers
when he is bitten by a radioactive spider

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:23.720
along with the Wild West-inspired Patrick
O'Hara, aka Web-Slinger, Widow's human partner.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:28.000
Miles also crosses paths with these characters
in the comics, even inducting them into his

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.470
Web-Warriors team at one point to fight a
Multiversal threat.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:35.020
Could a similar partnership form between these
characters in the movie?

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:39.600
Perhaps, but it looks like this majestic beast
of a Spider-Animal might be starting off on

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.819
the wrong foot with Miles ... or hoof, that
is.

00:07:42.819 --> 00:07:47.370
In any case, it's nice to see that Widow is
carrying on the Spider-Animal legacy for "Across

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.410
the Spider-Verse" — it's currently unknown
whether or not John Mulaney's Spider-Ham will

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.889
be making a return appearance.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:58.979
"Into the Spider-Verse" is full of great tunes,
but Blackway and Black Caviar's "What's Up

00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:02.330
Danger" is arguably the standout song of the
movie.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:07.159
The official trailer for "Across the Spider-Verse,"
released in December, also uses the song,

00:08:07.159 --> 00:08:08.320
carrying on its legacy.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:13.160
While two times might be a coincidence — or
in this case, a handy audio callback to the

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.930
greatness of the first "Spider-Verse" movie
— this second "Across the Spider-Verse"

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:22.870
trailer also uses "What's Up Danger" so very,
very prominently that the intention is clear.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:27.449
Every major superhero either has or would
greatly benefit from an instantly recognizable

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:28.659
theme song.

00:08:28.659 --> 00:08:32.969
This trailer goes a long way toward establishing
this track as an anthem for Miles.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.310
If you've spent any time on the internet at
all, you've almost certainly bumped into that

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:42.719
meme where two 1960s cartoon Spider-Man characters
are pointing at each other.

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:46.709
The good people at Sony and Marvel are well
aware of the popular image — to the point

00:08:46.709 --> 00:08:51.940
that in 2022, the official @SpiderManMovie
Twitter page even recreated it with "Spider-Man:

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:56.260
No Way Home" stars Tobey Maguire, Andrew Garfield,
and Tom Holland.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.450
The "Spider-Verse" people are also very familiar
with the meme.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:03.380
It popped up in the first film as a post-credits
sequence when we got our first look at Miguel

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:08.470
O'Hara, and the new trailer ramps the meme
up further than you might think was even possible.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:12.080
The trailer devotes but a few short seconds
to the gradual escalation of the pointing

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.840
scenario and the ensuing confusion, but it's
already hilarious enough to make the viewer

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:20.810
not-so-secretly hope that the full movie will
turn it into an extended gag.

